$DIR/test.p:7:10: enum type must be the type of a type definition: type E enum { ... }
    An enum type can only be the type of a type definition, type E enum { ... }.
    It cannot be written inline in a variable or field, or be an alias, because
    its members are reached through its name (E.Member).
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2301" for a longer explanation)
